<% seo title: "Privacy", description: "What Blendolo keeps, what Google sign in shares, who sees your photos, how long we keep them and how to delete everything at once." %>
<div class="page prose">
  <%= render "pages/page_header", chip: "Privacy", title: "Your photos, your call",
        lead: "No ads, no tracking, no passwords. Your kit lives behind a private link, and you can delete it all at once." %>

  <h2>What we keep</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your answers about your hands, and how your hands feel today.</li>
    <li>Your photos: today's photo, and an old photo if you choose to bring back a signature look.</li>
    <li>Colours read from your photo. Your phone reads them; we only keep the colour codes.</li>
    <li>The looks you pick, your routine and any share links you make.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>You can try the example people and start a kit without an account. We don't ask for your phone number.</p>

  <h2>Google sign in</h2>
  <p>To see looks on your own face, you sign in with Google. Your first look is free.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>We store your name, email and Google id, and the link to your Google picture. No passwords: Google checks who you are.</li>
    <li>We keep your credits: what you got and what each preview used.</li>
    <li>We ask Google for nothing else, and we don't share anything back with Google.</li>
    <li>The free credits come once per Google account. If you delete your account, we keep a one-way code made from your Google id so they aren't given twice. It can't be turned back into your id, your name or your email.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who sees your photos</h2>
  <p>YouCam, the try-on service from Perfect Corp, uses your photos to make the previews. It removes its copies within 30 days. Nobody else sees them unless you share a link that includes photos.</p>

  <h2>Code the photo page loads</h2>
  <p>On the photo page, your browser loads the face checking code from jsDelivr and the face model file from Google Cloud Storage. Like any website, they see your IP address. Your photo never goes to them: the checks run in your browser.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>30 days from your last visit, or 7 days if you choose that when you start. After that, your kit and its photos are deleted for good.</p>

  <h2>Delete everything</h2>
  <p>Every kit has a "Delete everything" button. It deletes your photos, answers and links at once. If you signed in, "Delete my account" on your account page deletes your account, all your kits and your credits at once. Our hourly database backups keep your answers, links and account details, not your photos, for up to 2 days after that. YouCam deletes its copies within 30 days.</p>

  <h2>Share links</h2>
  <p>You choose who a link is for and whether it shows photos. A link stops working after 30 days, and you can switch it off any time.</p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>Two small cookies, no trackers. One remembers your kit on this device so you can come back to it. The other keeps forms safe for up to 30 days and, if you sign in, keeps you signed in. Signing out ends it.</p>

  <h2>Payments</h2>
  <p>Dodo Payments is our merchant of record: when you buy credits, you pay them, and they handle your card, address and receipt under their own privacy policy. We never see your card. They tell us what was bought, when and for how much, with their ids for you as a customer and for each payment, so we can add your credits. We keep these payment records after you delete your account, without your name or email, for tax and accounting.</p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <%= render "pages/contact" %>
</div>
